   At datarates of 9600 or 12 000 bits/s, even without as-

suming severe channel distortions, the probability of symbol
error in unequalized transmission systems is very close to 1. It
is generally observed that decision-directedrecovery fails to
converge when theerrorprobability is in theorder of 0.1,
except in the case of purephase modulation.

   This exception has not been well understood so far, andwe
throw some light on this subject in the next section.

